TITLE:: EnhancedButton
SUMMARY:: A bordered button with label text and mouse-over / mouse-down colour styling.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/BorderView, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/Tuner

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::EnhancedButton:: is a subclass of LINK::Classes/BorderView:: that embeds a centred LINK::Classes/StaticText:: label. It provides default mouse-enter, mouse-leave, mouse-down, and mouse-up behaviour that updates background, border, and string colours, while still allowing custom mouse actions.

Set any of the following instance variables before interaction to customise appearance. Each may be left unset (nil) to leave that aspect unchanged during the corresponding interaction:

- TELETYPE::mouseEnterBackgroundColour::, TELETYPE::mouseEnterBorderColour::, TELETYPE::mouseEnterStringColour:: — applied while the pointer is over the button
- TELETYPE::mouseDownBackgroundColour::, TELETYPE::mouseDownBorderColour::, TELETYPE::mouseDownStringColour:: — applied while the mouse button is held down (takes precedence over enter colours)

When a colour is about to change, the current value is stored so it can be restored when the pointer leaves or the mouse button is released. TELETYPE::mouseDownAction_::, TELETYPE::mouseEnterAction_::, TELETYPE::mouseLeaveAction_::, and TELETYPE::mouseUpAction_:: each run the built-in styling first, then invoke the function you supply.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::EnhancedButton::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent view, or nil to create a top-level view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
The initial bounds as a LINK::Classes/Rect::, or nil for default layout sizing.

returns:: A new TELETYPE::EnhancedButton:: instance.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
PRIVATE:: init

METHOD:: align
The horizontal and vertical alignment of the label text (forwarded to the embedded LINK::Classes/StaticText::). Set with TELETYPE::align_::.

returns:: The current alignment.

METHOD:: font
The font used for the label text (forwarded to the embedded LINK::Classes/StaticText::). Set with TELETYPE::font_::.

returns:: The current font.

METHOD:: mouseDownAction_
Sets the function called on mouse-down, after the default down-state colours are applied.

ARGUMENT:: func
A function of three arguments: view, x, y.

METHOD:: mouseEnterAction_
Sets the function called when the pointer enters the button, after the default enter-state colours are applied.

ARGUMENT:: func
A function of three arguments: view, x, y.

METHOD:: mouseLeaveAction_
Sets the function called when the pointer leaves the button, after the default colours are restored.

ARGUMENT:: func
A function of three arguments: view, x, y.

METHOD:: mouseUpAction_
Sets the function called on mouse-up, after the default up-state colours are applied.

ARGUMENT:: func
A function of three arguments: view, x, y.

METHOD:: string
The label text (forwarded to the embedded LINK::Classes/StaticText::). Set with TELETYPE::string_::.

returns:: The current string.

METHOD:: stringColor
The label text colour (forwarded to the embedded LINK::Classes/StaticText::). Set with TELETYPE::stringColor_::.

returns:: The current colour.


EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var palette = GuiPalette.default;
var button = EnhancedButton()
	.background_(palette.colour3)
	.borderRadius_(3)
	.borderWidth_(2)
	.minSize_(100@50)
	.font_(Font(size: 16))
	.string_("OK")
	.stringColor_(palette.colour5)
	.align_(\center)
	.mouseEnterBorderColour_(palette.extreme2)
	.mouseEnterStringColour_(palette.extreme2)
	.mouseDownBackgroundColour_(palette.colour2)
	.mouseUpAction_({ "clicked".postln; });
)
::
